{"type":"message","id":"e3cf54b7","parentId":"9dcd815e","timestamp":"2026-03-04T02:27:09.093Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Wed 2026-03-04 10:27 GMT+8] [Subagent Context] You are running as a subagent (depth 1/2). Results auto-announce to your requester; do not busy-poll for status.\n\n[Subagent Task]: ## 任务：开发协作像素编辑器 (Pixel Art Editor with CRDTs)\n\n### 工作目录\n`/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor`\n\n### 项目概述\n基于 Jake Lazaroff 的教程系列，开发一个使用 CRDT 的协作像素编辑器。\n\n参考文章：\n- Part 1: https://jakelazaroff.com/words/an-interactive-intro-to-crdts/\n- Part 2: https://jakelazaroff.com/words/building-a-collaborative-pixel-art-editor-with-crdts/\n- Part 3: https://jakelazaroff.com/words/making-crdts-98-percent-more-efficient/\n\n需求文档已创建：`/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor/REQUIREMENTS.md`\n\n### 开发阶段\n\n**Phase 1: Core CRDTs**\n- LWWRegister.ts\n- LWWMap.ts\n- PixelData.ts\n- 基础单元测试\n\n**Phase 2: Pixel Editor UI**\n- Canvas 渲染\n- 指针事件处理\n- DDA 线条绘制算法\n\n**Phase 3: State Synchronization**\n- 状态交换机制\n- 网络模拟（延迟/断网）\n- 时间戳优化\n\n**Phase 4: Binary Encoding (98% compression)**\n- Hex codes\n- UUID/Palette 表去重\n- 游程编码\n- 二进制格式\n\n**Phase 5: Testing & Polish**\n- 完整测试覆盖\n- 性能基准\n- 文档\n\n### 技术要求\n- TypeScript (strict mode)\n- ES modules\n- 无外部依赖（Phase 1-3）\n- Canvas 2D API\n- Pointer Events API\n\n### 团队分工\n- **search-agent**: 研究技术细节、CRDT 最佳实践\n- **design-agent**: 架构设计、接口定义\n- **code-agent**: 核心代码实现\n- **test-agent**: 单元测试、集成测试\n- **review-agent**: 代码审查、质量把控\n- **docs-agent**: 文档编写\n\n### 工作流程\n1. design-agent 设计架构 → 确认后进入开发\n2. code-agent 实现 → test-agent 测试 → review-agent 审查\n3. 发现问题 → 循环迭代（最多 3 次）\n4. 完成 Phase → 进入下一 Phase\n\n### 输出要求\n每个 Phase 结束后输出综合报告到 `$HOME/.openclaw-reports/leader-agent/`\n\n完成后向我汇报进度。"}],"timestamp":1772591229090}}
{"type":"message","id":"b6e75390","parentId":"e3cf54b7","timestamp":"2026-03-04T02:27:20.450Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user has assigned me a task to develop a collaborative pixel art editor with CRDTs. Let me follow the AGENTS.md workflow:\n\n## Phase 0: Confirm Workspace ⚠️\nWorkspace is clearly specified: `/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor`\n\n## Phase 1: Understand Requirements\nLet me first read the requirements document to understand what needs to be done.\n\nThe task is complex:\n- New architecture (CRDT-based collaboration)\n- Multiple components (Core CRDTs, UI, Sync, Binary encoding)\n- Unknown technology details (need to research CRDTs)\n- Significant user-facing changes\n\nThis is a **Complex** task.\n\n## Selected Team:\n- search-agent: Research CRDTs, best practices\n- design-agent: Architecture design\n- code-agent: Implementation\n- test-agent: Testing\n- review-agent: Code review\n- docs-agent: Documentation\n\n## Workflow DAG:\n```\nsearch-agent → design-agent → code-agent → test-agent → review-agent → docs-agent\n                                ↑              │\n                                └──────────────┘ (loop if issues, max 3x)\n```\n\nLet me start by reading the requirements document to understand what's already defined.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"我来按照 AGENTS.md 的工作流程协调开发任务。\n\n## Phase 0: 确认工作目录\n**工作目录确认:** `/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor` ✅\n\n## Phase 1: 理解需求\n\n首先让我读取已有的需求文档："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-9b3e12ccb89344d6a335449b88afdaef","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor/REQUIREMENTS.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-61811c732a2e468cbec93bed0c57cb49","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"ls -la /home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor/ 2>/dev/null || echo \"Directory not found\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":12762,"output":609,"cacheRead":253,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":13624,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772591229093}}
{"type":"message","id":"25ad2ffb","parentId":"b6e75390","timestamp":"2026-03-04T02:27:20.462Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool-9b3e12ccb89344d6a335449b88afdaef","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Pixel Art Editor - Requirements\n\n## Project Overview\n\nBuild a **collaborative pixel art editor** using CRDTs (Conflict-free Replicated Data Types). Based on Jake Lazaroff's tutorial series:\n- Part 1: https://jakelazaroff.com/words/an-interactive-intro-to-crdts/\n- Part 2: https://jakelazaroff.com/words/building-a-collaborative-pixel-art-editor-with-crdts/\n- Part 3: https://jakelazaroff.com/words/making-crdts-98-percent-more-efficient/\n\n## Core Features\n\n### 1. CRDT Data Structures\n\n#### LWWRegister<T>\n- Stores a single value with peer ID, timestamp, and value tuple\n- Merge logic: higher timestamp wins; ties broken by peer ID comparison\n- `set(value)` increments local timestamp\n\n#### LWWMap<T>\n- Wraps multiple LWWRegisters, one per key\n- Methods: `get`, `set`, `delete`, `has`, `merge`\n- Tombstones for deletions (set to null, not remove key)\n- Value type filters out null values\n\n#### PixelData\n- Thin wrapper over LWWMap<RGB>\n- Key method: `static key(x, y)` returns `\"x,y\"` string\n- Default color: white [255, 255, 255]\n- RGB type: `[red: number, green: number, blue: number]`\n\n### 2. Pixel Editor UI\n\n#### Canvas Setup\n- Two canvases (simulating two peers)\n- Artboard size: configurable (e.g., 100x100)\n- Canvas element size: separate from artboard (e.g., 400x400)\n- Handle devicePixelRatio for crisp pixels\n- Crosshair cursor, touch-action: none\n\n#### Drawing\n- Pointer events: pointerdown, pointermove, pointerup\n- Pointer capture for continuous drag\n- Coordinate conversion: canvas pixels → artboard pixels\n- Line drawing with DDA (Digital Differential Analyzer) algorithm\n- Prevent gaps when moving cursor quickly\n\n#### Color Input\n- HTML `<input type=\"color\">` for color picker\n- Convert hex code to RGB: `\"#6c4fff\"` → `[108, 79, 255]`\n\n### 3. State Synchronization\n\n#### Network Simulation\n- Toggle network on/off\n- Adjustable latency (via setTimeout)\n- When network off: local changes don't sync\n- When network on: states merge automatically\n\n#### State Exchange\n- `onchange` listener: fires when local state changes\n- `receive(state)`: merge remote state, redraw canvas\n- Full state sync on each change\n\n### 4. Timestamp Optimization\n\nProblem: rapid pointer events increment timestamps excessively\n\nSolution:\n- Track painted pixels during a drag operation (`Set<string>`)\n- Skip setting pixel if already painted in current drag\n- Clear set on pointerup\n\n### 5. Binary Encoding (Part 3 - Optimization)\n\n#### Compression Pipeline\n1. **Hex codes**: RGB tuples → hex strings (6% reduction)\n2. **UUID table**: Deduplicate peer IDs (63% reduction)\n3. **Palette table**: Deduplicate colors (71% reduction)\n4. **Run-length encoding**: Compress blank pixels (80% reduction)\n5. **Binary encoding**: Custom binary format (~94% reduction)\n6. **Run-length binary**: Split data chunks (98% reduction)\n\n#### Binary Format Structure\n```\nINFO chunk: \"CRDT\" magic + artboard width\nUUID chunk: \"UUID\" header + deduplicated peer IDs (16 bytes each)\nPLTT chunk: \"PLTT\" header + color palette (3 bytes each)\nTIME chunk: \"TIME\" header + timestamps (run-length encoded)\nWRTR chunk: \"WRTR\" header + writer IDs (run-length encoded)\nCOLR chunk: \"COLR\" header + color indices (run-length encoded)\n```\n\n## Technical Constraints\n\n### Language\n- TypeScript (strict mode recommended)\n- ES modules\n\n### Browser APIs\n- Canvas 2D API\n- Pointer Events API\n- createImageBitmap + ImageData\n\n### No External Libraries (Phase 1)\n- Build CRDTs from scratch for learning\n- Optional: use CRDT libraries for production\n\n## Deliverables\n\n1. **Core CRDT Library** (`src/crdt/`)\n   - LWWRegister.ts\n   - LWWMap.ts\n   - PixelData.ts\n\n2. **Editor UI** (`src/editor/`)\n   - PixelEditor.ts\n   - Canvas rendering\n   - Event handling\n   - Line drawing\n\n3. **Demo Page** (`index.html`, `style.css`, `main.ts`)\n   - Two canvas demo\n   - Network toggle\n   - Latency slider\n   - Color picker\n\n4. **Binary Encoding** (`src/encoding/`)\n   - Encoder.ts (state → binary)\n   - Decoder.ts (binary → state)\n   - All compression stages\n\n5. **Tests** (`tests/`)\n   - Unit tests for CRDTs\n   - Merge behavior tests\n   - Encoding/decoding roundtrip tests\n\n## Development Phases\n\n### Phase 1: Core CRDTs\n- Implement LWWRegister\n- Implement LWWMap\n- Basic tests\n\n### Phase 2: Pixel Editor\n- Canvas setup\n- Drawing logic\n- Line drawing (DDA)\n\n### Phase 3: Synchronization\n- State exchange\n- Network simulation\n- Timestamp optimization\n\n### Phase 4: Binary Encoding\n- Hex codes\n- UUID/Palette tables\n- Run-length encoding\n- Binary format\n\n### Phase 5: Testing & Polish\n- Comprehensive tests\n- Performance benchmarks\n- Documentation\n\n## File Structure\n\n```\n/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor/\n├── src/\n│   ├── crdt/\n│   │   ├── LWWRegister.ts\n│   │   ├── LWWMap.ts\n│   │   └── PixelData.ts\n│   ├── editor/\n│   │   └── PixelEditor.ts\n│   ├── encoding/\n│   │   ├── Encoder.ts\n│   │   └── Decoder.ts\n│   └── types.ts\n├── tests/\n│   ├── LWWRegister.test.ts\n│   ├── LWWMap.test.ts\n│   └── encoding.test.ts\n├── index.html\n├── style.css\n├── main.ts\n├── package.json\n├── tsconfig.json\n└── REQUIREMENTS.md\n```\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- [ ] Two canvases can draw independently\n- [ ] States sync when network is on\n- [ ] Offline changes merge correctly when back online\n- [ ] Timestamp conflicts resolved correctly\n- [ ] Smooth line drawing (no gaps)\n- [ ] Binary encoding achieves >90% compression\n- [ ] All tests pass"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1772591240459}}
