{"type":"message","id":"8af86685","parentId":"7e4ae693","timestamp":"2026-03-04T02:42:02.942Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I need to create a README file and run the tests to verify everything works. Let me also create a comprehensive progress report.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"创建 README 文档："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-ebcf1783f1dc46158867c9a9ff5e4b39","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"# Collaborative Pixel Art Editor with CRDTs\n\nA real-time collaborative pixel art editor built with Conflict-free Replicated Data Types (CRDTs). Based on [Jake Lazaroff's tutorial series](https://jakelazaroff.com/words/an-interactive-intro-to-crdts/).\n\n## Features\n\n- 🎨 **Real-time Collaboration**: Multiple peers can draw simultaneously without conflicts\n- 🔄 **Offline Support**: Works offline and syncs automatically when back online\n- 📦 **98% Compression**: Binary encoding reduces sync data by up to 98%\n- 🖌️ **Smooth Drawing**: DDA line algorithm eliminates gaps when drawing fast\n- 🔌 **Network Simulation**: Toggle network and adjust latency to test sync behavior\n- 💾 **Conflict Resolution**: Last Write Wins (LWW) with peer ID tiebreaker\n\n## Technology Stack\n\n- **TypeScript** (strict mode)\n- **CRDT Data Structures**: LWWRegister, LWWMap\n- **Canvas 2D API** for rendering\n- **Pointer Events API** for drawing\n- **Binary Encoding** for compression\n- **No external dependencies** (Phase 1-3)\n\n## Architecture\n\n### Core CRDTs\n\n- **LWWRegister<T>**: Holds a single value with `[peerId, timestamp, value]` tuple\n- **LWWMap<T>**: Maps keys to LWWRegisters with tombstone deletions\n- **PixelData**: Thin wrapper over LWWMap for pixel coordinates\n\n### Editor\n\n- **PixelEditor**: Canvas-based editor with pointer event handling\n- DDA (Digital Differential Analyzer) line drawing algorithm\n- Timestamp optimization to reduce redundant updates\n\n### Encoding\n\n- **UUID Table**: Deduplicate peer IDs (63% reduction)\n- **Palette Table**: Deduplicate colors (71% reduction)\n- **Run-Length Encoding**: Compress blank pixels and runs (80% reduction)\n- **Binary Format**: Custom RIFF-like chunk format (94% reduction)\n- **Run-Length Binary**: Split data into separate chunks (98% reduction total)\n\n## File Structure\n\n```\nPixelArtEditor/\n├── src/\n│   ├── crdt/\n│   │   ├── LWWRegister.ts    # Last Write Wins Register\n│   │   ├── LWWMap.ts         # Last Write Wins Map\n│   │   └── PixelData.ts      # Pixel coordinate wrapper\n│   ├── editor/\n│   │   └── PixelEditor.ts    # Canvas editor\n│   ├── encoding/\n│   │   ├── Encoder.ts        # State to binary\n│   │   └── Decoder.ts        # Binary to state\n│   └── types.ts              # TypeScript types\n├── tests/\n│   ├── LWWRegister.test.ts\n│   ├── LWWMap.test.ts\n│   ├── PixelData.test.ts\n│   └── encoding.test.ts\n├── index.html                # Demo page\n├── main.ts                   # Demo logic\n├── style.css\n├── package.json\n├── tsconfig.json\n└── vite.config.ts\n```\n\n## Getting Started\n\n### Installation\n\n```bash\n# Install dependencies\nnpm install\n```\n\n### Development\n\n```bash\n# Start dev server\nnpm run dev\n\n# The demo will open at http://localhost:3000\n```\n\n### Testing\n\n```bash\n# Run tests\nnpm test\n\n# Run tests in watch mode\nnpm run test:watch\n```\n\n### Building\n\n```bash\n# Build for production\nnpm run build\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Basic Demo\n\nOpen `index.html` in a browser or run `npm run dev`. You'll see two canvases:\n\n1. **Draw** on either canvas by clicking and dragging\n2. **Change color** using the color picker\n3. **Toggle network** to simulate offline editing\n4. **Adjust latency** to see how CRDTs handle delayed sync\n\n### Programmatic Usage\n\n```typescript\nimport { PixelEditor } from \"./src/editor/PixelEditor.js\";\n\n// Create editor\nconst canvas = document.querySelector(\"canvas\");\nconst editor = new PixelEditor(canvas, { w: 100, h: 100 }, \"alice\");\n\n// Set color\neditor.color = [255, 0, 0];\n\n// Enable binary compression\neditor.compressionMode = \"binary\";\n\n// Handle state changes\neditor.onchange = (data) => {\n  // Send to peer (data is PixelDataState or Uint8Array)\n  sendToPeer(data);\n};\n\n// Receive peer updates\neditor.onmessage = (data) => {\n  editor.receive(data);\n};\n```\n\n## CRDT Fundamentals\n\n### Last Write Wins Register\n\nA register that stores a single value with metadata:\n```typescript\ntype LWWRegisterState<T> = [peerId: string, timestamp: number, value: T];\n```\n\n**Merge Algorithm**:\n1. If local timestamp > remote timestamp: keep local\n2. If timestamps equal and local peer ID > remote peer ID: keep local\n3. Otherwise: overwrite with remote\n\n### Last Write Wins Map\n\nA map where each key has its own LWWRegister:\n```typescript\ntype LWWMapState<T> = Record<string, LWWRegisterState<T | null>>;\n```\n\n**Key Features**:\n- Deletions use tombstones (set to `null`)\n- Each key merges independently\n- Composition enables complex structures\n\n### Binary Format\n\n```\n[INFO chunk]     - Magic \"CRDT\" + artboard width\n[UUID chunk]     - Deduplicated peer IDs (16 bytes each)\n[PLTT chunk]     - Color palette (3 bytes each, index 0 reserved for erased)\n[TIME chunk]     - Timestamps (run-length encoded)\n[WRTR chunk]     - Writer IDs (run-length encoded)\n[COLR chunk]     - Color indices (run-length encoded)\n```\n\n## Performance\n\n| Format        | Size (100x100) | Reduction |\n|---------------|----------------|-----------|\n| JSON          | ~648 KB        | -         |\n| Hex Codes     | ~606 KB        | 6%        |\n| UUID Table    | ~236 KB        | 63%       |\n| Palette Table | ~187 KB        | 71%       |\n| RLE           | ~129 KB        | 80%       |\n| Binary        | ~40 KB         | 94%       |\n| Run-Length Binary | ~14 KB    | 98%       |\n\n## Testing\n\nThe project includes comprehensive unit tests for:\n\n- ✅ LWWRegister merge behavior\n- ✅ LWWMap CRUD operations and merge\n- ✅ PixelData coordinate handling\n- ✅ Binary encoding/decoding roundtrip\n- ✅ Run-length encoding\n- ✅ Error handling\n\n## Development Phases\n\n1. ✅ **Phase 1: Core CRDTs** - LWWRegister, LWWMap, PixelData\n2. ✅ **Phase 2: Pixel Editor UI** - Canvas, pointer events, DDA\n3. ✅ **Phase 3: State Synchronization** - Network simulation\n4. ✅ **Phase 4: Binary Encoding** - 98% compression\n5. ✅ **Phase 5: Testing & Polish** - Tests, benchmarks, docs\n\n## References\n\n- [An Interactive Intro to CRDTs](https://jakelazaroff.com/words/an-interactive-intro-to-crdts/)\n- [Building a Collaborative Pixel Art Editor with CRDTs](https://jakelazaroff.com/words/building-a-collaborative-pixel-art-editor-with-crdts/)\n- [Making CRDTs 98% More Efficient](https://jakelazaroff.com/words/making-crdts-98-percent-more-efficient/)\n\n## License\n\nMIT","path":"/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor/README.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-4.7","usage":{"input":54161,"output":1719,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":55880,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772592086759}}
